From 6291d495e932c7641c1e2f9564c259db29787635 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:21:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Kanban churn guards: cap parent handoffs in worker
 context, wait-comment --from-card, tell a commenter when a parked card will
 not wake

Three causes of card churn measured on 2026-11-18 (t_c850e0f6, t_5f0d878cd1c10371, t_0b716b01a47db7f6):

- Worker context: done-parent handoffs are capped at the 8 most recently completed; older ones are named in
  one line. Long-lived owner cards had 22 and 30 finished prerequisites linked (51 KB and 42 KB of ~100 KB).
  Cards with 8 or fewer done parents are unchanged.
- wait-comment --from-card <task id>: wake on a comment written by one card's worker instead of a phrase the
  other card has to reproduce. A worker commenting on another card now records writer_task on the commented
  event (workers share a profile, so the author cannot say); a relay author <gateway>/<task id> also matches.
- kanban comment (CLI and the kanban_comment tool) says when the target is scheduled on a probe made only of
  wait-comment alternatives on that card and this comment satisfies none. A request worded 'bounded SOURCE
  GO REQUEST' sat five hours against a probe wanting 'BOUNDED exact-head SOURCE GO REQUEST'.

Limits: the note is given only where the board holding the comment also holds the card's wake check (its
home). Any probe with &&, ;, a pipe, a subshell, a negation, another command or raw SQL is never judged.
Comments written before this change carry no writer_task, so --from-card sees only their author spelling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
